# Source: HoareLogic.pdf, section "Exercises", "Reading from arrays", item 2.
id: array-read
title: Reading two neighbouring cells
topic: Arrays
level: 2
source: HoareLogic.pdf, Exercises, "Reading from arrays" 2
tags: arrays, array read, definedness

task:
  Compute the weakest precondition with the rule ARRAY-READ. Unfold the
  definedness conditions and simplify the result. Show that the two
  definedness conditions can be written as the single condition
  $0 <= i && i + 1 < sizeof(a)$.

pre: a[i] >= a[i + 1] && 0 <= i && i + 1 < sizeof(a)
post: x >= 0

program:
  {P}
  {R1}
  x := a[i] - a[i + 1]
  {Q}

verdict: valid

step: Substitute, as in the assignment rule
rule: ARRAY-READ, WP
focus: x :=
calc:
  (x >= 0)[x <- a[i] - a[i + 1]]
  = a[i] - a[i + 1] >= 0
  = a[i] >= a[i + 1]            // add a[i + 1] to both sides

step: Add one definedness condition per read
rule: ARRAY-READ
text:
  The expression reads the array twice, at $i$ and at $i + 1$. Each read
  gets its condition, and each condition is about the whole index
  expression.
calc:
  wp(x := a[i] - a[i + 1], Q)
  = a[i] - a[i + 1] >= 0 && def(a[i]) && def(a[i + 1])
  = a[i] >= a[i + 1] && 0 <= i < sizeof(a) && 0 <= i + 1 < sizeof(a)
set: R1 = a[i] >= a[i + 1] && 0 <= i < sizeof(a) && 0 <= i + 1 < sizeof(a)

step: Merge the two definedness conditions
rule: LOGIC
calc:
  0 <= i < sizeof(a) && 0 <= i + 1 < sizeof(a)
  = 0 <= i && i + 1 < sizeof(a)
text:
  From left to right: $0 <= i$ is in the first condition and
  $i + 1 < sizeof(a)$ in the second. From right to left: $0 <= i$ gives
  $0 <= i + 1$, and $i + 1 < sizeof(a)$ gives $i < sizeof(a)$.
vc: a[i] >= a[i + 1] && 0 <= i && i + 1 < sizeof(a) ==> R1
result: The weakest precondition is $a[i] >= a[i + 1] && 0 <= i && i + 1 < sizeof(a)$.

summary:
  The two reads $a[i]$ and $a[i + 1]$ must both be inside the array. Since
  $i + 1$ is the larger index, it decides the upper bound, and $i$ decides
  the lower bound.
